does it COMPILE?
  (?R)     no
  (?1)     no
  (?&par)  no
  \g<0>    yes
  \g<1>    yes
  \g<par>  yes

\g<0>, unanchored
  (a(b)c)    found '(a(b)c)'
  ((a)(b))   found '((a)(b))'
  ()         found '()'
  (a(b)c     found '(b)'
  a          no match

\A...\g<0>...\z -- the anchors are INSIDE the recursion
  (a(b)c)    no match
  ((a)(b))   no match
  ()         match
  (a(b)c     no match
  a          no match

\g<1> and \g<par>, anchored
  (a(b)c)    by number match     by name match
  ((a)(b))   by number match     by name match
  ()         by number match     by name match
  (a(b)c     by number no match  by name no match
  a          by number no match  by name no match

nesting depth, with the \g<1> form
  depth 1     match
  depth 10    match
  depth 100   match
  depth 1000  match
